  "mechanisms": [
    "Socio-cultural currents influence the formation of dominant personality traits in people.",
    "Personality traits play a decisive role in shaping individuals' perceptual-cognitive systems, mental schemas, and cognitive maps.",
    "Mental schemas and cognitive maps provide individuals with a different understanding and perception of the environment.",
    "Environmental affordances are evaluated and exploited based on personality traits, leading to the realization of environmental meaning.",
    "Perception of physical meanings (explicit) and abstract meanings (implicit/symbolic) leads to semantic presence and strong connection with the environment, creating a sense of place."
  ],
  "moderators": [
    "socio-cultural indicators of society",
    "users' personality traits"
  ],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "Architectural design should consider region-specified users' psychological personality types to effectively design spaces, achieve desired sense of place, and improve quality of life.",
    "Design processes should identify and determine different perceptions based on culture and personality traits to promote a sense of place.",
    "A structured framework can guide the design process to adapt spatial features to perceptual-cognitive dimensions and basic human needs.",
    "POE can be used to identify problems and weaknesses in existing buildings and improve their current condition.",
    "Results can inform evidence-based design strategies for future projects, increasing user satisfaction, performance, and sense of place attachment.",
    "Designing based on these findings can increase users' mental health, influence spatial behaviors positively, reduce repair/renovation costs, and improve cultural levels and social characteristics of the community."
  ],
